//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class
// $Module name: cWin32ProjectionHarvester
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-08-28
//
// Description : MAINTAINER TOOL ENGINE - the DataFlex port of Tools\HarvestWin32Projection.py.
//
//               Reads a local clone of Win32_DataFlex_Projection (Frank Cheng, MIT - generated
//               from Microsoft's win32metadata) and merges "DF|"-flavoured rows into
//               Data\WinAPICatalog.json and Data\WinAPIStructCatalog.json. The Python tool's
//               contract is ported rule for rule; where a rule has a WHY, it is restated here so
//               this file stands alone:
//
//               INTERSECTION, NOT ALL 18,300. The Deep Scan runs one catalogue lookup per
//               External_Function declaration, so the working set is the entry points the
//               corpus scan actually found (AppSrc\WindowsAPI.json); pbHarvestAll opts into
//               everything, accepting the cost knowingly.
//
//               HOW WELL THE PROJECTION FITS REAL LEGACY CODE (measured 2026-08-28, before the
//               first harvest; kept here because it cannot be re-derived from this repo). About
//               thirty real legacy workspaces of 1990s-2010s production code were scanned for
//               every External_Function they declare: 1,310 distinct Windows entry points across
//               ~17,700 declarations. The projection covers 98% of those entry points and over
//               99% of the declarations; the only misses were the winspool family and
//               GlobalDiscard. That number is why this catalogue is worth maintaining at all -
//               and it is the yardstick for any future claim that some other source would serve
//               better.
//
//               NORMALISATION:
//                 * Pointer -> Handle where the projection's C comment names a handle type
//                   (H[A-Z0-9_]+, excluding HRESULT/HFILE which are integers). Legacy code says
//                   Handle; harvesting Pointer verbatim would make the retyper churn it.
//                 * VOID returns arrive SPELLED, and are kept that way. Upstream cec3389
//                   (2026-08-30) made void explicit as "Returns Void_Type" - which is real
//                   DataFlex, declared that way by Winkern.pkg and MapiDllCalls.Pkg in the
//                   install - so there is nothing left to infer. An explicit "// void" comment
//                   normalises to that same spelling, so the catalogue says void exactly one way.
//                   A bare, uncommented "Returns Pointer" is now left ALONE. It used to mean
//                   void (verified across all 1,384 bare rows at head 7319adc) and was mapped to
//                   Returns Integer, after harvesting it verbatim broke every call site storing
//                   the meaningless result (WinServ KeyStroke, 2026-08-28). That inference is
//                   retired with the shape it read: at cec3389 there are ZERO bare rows and all
//                   1,427 pointer returns carry their C type, so a bare row reappearing would be
//                   a genuine pointer whose comment has not landed yet - and calling it Integer
//                   would truncate an address on x64, the very defect this tool hunts. Guessing
//                   wrong toward Pointer merely declines to improve a declaration.
//                 * Function declarations flatten to ONE line (the consumers' contract);
//                   struct bodies KEEP their newlines (member boundaries are meaningful).
//
//               STRUCT CLOSURE: a harvested function pulls the structs its comments name, and
//               each struct pulls the struct types among its members - FILETIME arrives because
//               WIN32_FIND_DATAW carries three of them. Nothing else, without pbHarvestAll.
//
//               WITH pbHarvestAll, EVERY NAMED STRUCT (2026-11-04). The closure can never reach what
//               travels through SendMessage's lParam and WM_NOTIFY: no prototype names NMHDR,
//               NMLISTVIEW, LVHITTESTINFO or TVITEM. Reaching them takes a clone at 8c132ef or later;
//               cec3389 (2026-08-29) translated only the structs its APIs needed, 2,892 of them and
//               none of those. Measured at 8c132ef: 15,206 structs, of which 12,785 named.
//
//               A NAME THE PROJECTION MADE UP IS NOT HARVESTED (_IsGeneratedStructName). From
//               8c132ef on, a union or an anonymous nested struct is a type of its own, numbered
//               in generation order: _Anonymous_e__Union_2975. No source can name one, the number
//               moves with every regeneration, and DataFlex ships no twin to emit it as. A row that
//               has such a member is still harvested, because its name and its first members are
//               real; the converter cannot write it, so a Type that names it keeps its own member types.
//
//               MERGE: a harvested FUNCTION (dll|entry) replaces the existing row. A harvested
//               STRUCT (NAME) never does, it is only added (_RowsNotCarried): 8c132ef rewrites 331
//               of the rows this catalogue holds, most of them from a byte block every consumer
//               can read to one of those numbered types nothing can. To take a newer row on
//               purpose, delete the old one first. Every identity the harvest does not carry -
//               the winspool family, hand-added rows - stays untouched. Re-running is idempotent.
//               Rows are written KEY-sorted (the same order the Python tool wrote, so a re-run
//               diffs clean); the funclib re-sorts on load anyway, so file order is cosmetic.
//
//               ALL PATHS ARE EXPLICIT PARAMETERS so the unit tests never touch the real files,
//               exactly as cWinAPICatalogStore does.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use vWin32fh.pkg                 // vFolderFormat / vFilePathExists
Use cEncodingHelpers.pkg         // rfFileSize - RefactorFileIO needs it defined first
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg           // rfFileSearchRecursive / rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray / channel I/O
Use cJsonObject.pkg
Use JsonEnhancement.pkg          // MemberEnh / MemberValueEnh
Use cWinAPICatalogStore.pkg      // LoadCatalog - the ONE reader for the catalogue files

/* The one Windows call the alias measurement makes (2026-09-12, see BareAliasRows). GetProcAddress
   has no A/W twin of its own and takes an ANSI name, so String is right; it answers a CODE ADDRESS,
   so LongPtr is right on both bitnesses and ONE declaration covers them. LoadLibrary comes from the
   install (Winkern.pkg); nothing is freed - a system dll that answered once stays mapped for the
   run, and this is a maintainer tool that exits straight after. */
External_Function HarvGetProcAddress "GetProcAddress" Kernel32.dll ;
    Handle hModule String lpProcName Returns LongPtr

// One parsed projection function. Parallel param arrays are written in lockstep by the one
// parser below and never elsewhere.
Struct tW32ProjFn
    String   sName
    String   sEntry
    String   sDll
    String[] asParamType
    String[] asParamName
    String[] asParamComment
    String   sRet
    String   sRetComment
End_Struct

Class cWin32ProjectionHarvester is a cObject

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        // --all: harvest every projection function and every named struct, instead of the corpus
        // intersection and the structs it reaches.
        Property Boolean pbHarvestAll False
    End_Procedure

    // Whitespace-split into non-blank tokens (tabs count as whitespace).
    Procedure _Tokens String sText String[] ByRef asTok
        String[] asRaw asNone
        Integer i iLast

        Move asNone to asTok
        Move (Replaces((Character(9)), sText, " ")) to sText
        Move (StrSplitToArray(Trim(sText), " ")) to asRaw
        Move (SizeOfArray(asRaw) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Trim(asRaw[i]) <> "") ;
                Move (Trim(asRaw[i])) to asTok[SizeOfArray(asTok)]
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // The C comment names a HANDLE type: 'H' then uppercase letters/digits/underscores, a
    // trailing '*' tolerated. HRESULT and HFILE look the part and are integers - excluded by
    // list, not pattern. Case-sensitive on purpose: the projection writes C type names.
    Function _IsHandleComment String sComment Returns Boolean
        String sC sCh
        Integer i iLen iAsc

        Move (Trim(sComment)) to sC
        While (Right(sC, 1) = "*")
            Move (Trim(Left(sC, (Length(sC) - 1)))) to sC
        Loop
        Move (Length(sC)) to iLen
        If (iLen < 2) ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Ascii(Left(sC, 1)) <> 72) ;                      // 'H', exactly - case-sensitive
            Function_Return False
        For i from 2 to iLen
            Move (Mid(sC, 1, i)) to sCh
            Move (Ascii(sCh)) to iAsc
            If (not((iAsc >= 65 and iAsc <= 90) or (iAsc >= 48 and iAsc <= 57) or sCh = "_")) ;
                Function_Return False
        Loop
        If (sC = "HRESULT" or sC = "HFILE") ;
            Function_Return False
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    Function NormaliseType String sType String sComment Returns String
        If (sType = "Pointer" and _IsHandleComment(Self, sComment)) ;
            Function_Return "Handle"
        Function_Return sType
    End_Function

    // Void is SPELLED upstream now, not inferred from a bare Pointer (see the header). An
    // explicit "// void" comment - one of the two remedies the 2026-08-28 issue proposed, and
    // not the one Frank took - normalises to the same Void_Type the generator emits, so the
    // catalogue never carries two spellings of one fact for _IsVoidApiReturn to have to know.
    Function NormaliseReturn String sType String sComment Returns String
        If (Lowercase(Trim(sComment)) = "void") ;
            Function_Return "Void_Type"
        Function_Return (NormaliseType(Self, sType, sComment))
    End_Function

    // Tokens iFrom.. joined with single spaces (the multi-token parameter-name case).
    Function JoinTokensFrom String[] ByRef asTok Integer iFrom Returns String
        String sOut
        Integer i iLast

        Move "" to sOut
        Move (SizeOfArray(asTok) - 1) to iLast
        For i from iFrom to iLast
            If (sOut = "") ;
                Move asTok[i] to sOut
            Else ;
                Move (sOut + " " + asTok[i]) to sOut
        Loop
        Function_Return sOut
    End_Function

    // Word-shaped, the original tool's \w+ : letters, digits and underscores only. The clone
    // holds exactly one ordinal-named declaration ('External_Function #660 "#660" SHELL32.dll',
    // FileIconInit, still there at cec3389) - the original tool rejected it and so does this.
    //
    // NOT because it fails to compile. It was long assumed "#660 cannot be a DataFlex
    // identifier"; measured 2026-08-30, DataFlex 26 accepts it in BOTH the declaration and the
    // call site ("Move (#660(1)) to iX" builds), with a deliberate bad symbol in the same file
    // still raising Error 4328 - so the compile really was exercised. The skip stands on its own
    // merit: an ordinal-only export has no name for a legacy declaration to match against, which
    // is the only thing this catalogue is for.
    Function _IsWordName String sName Returns Boolean
        String sCh
        Integer i iLen iAsc

        Move (Length(sName)) to iLen
        If (iLen = 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        For i from 1 to iLen
            Move (Mid(sName, 1, i)) to sCh
            Move (Ascii(sCh)) to iAsc
            If (not((iAsc >= 65 and iAsc <= 90) or (iAsc >= 97 and iAsc <= 122) or (iAsc >= 48 and iAsc <= 57) or sCh = "_")) ;
                Function_Return False
        Loop
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    // Linear exact-match contains (small arrays; the sorted variant serves the big ones).
    Function _PlainContains String[] ByRef asList String sKey Returns Boolean
        Integer i iLast
        Move (SizeOfArray(asList) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (asList[i] = sKey) ;
                Function_Return True
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    /* A struct name the projection generated rather than Windows declaring it: "_Anonymous_e__Union_2975",
       "_BitField_1843", "__DummyPinType__". Windows' own names with a leading underscore (_URB_HEADER, __UPV)
       are not. PURE. */
    Function _IsGeneratedStructName String sName Returns Boolean
        String sTail
        Integer iAt i iLast

        If (Left(sName, 1) <> "_") ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Pos("_e__", Lowercase(sName)) > 0) ;
            Function_Return True
        If (Left(sName, 2) = "__" and Right(sName, 2) = "__") ;
            Function_Return True
        Move (RightPos("_", sName)) to iAt
        Move (Right(sName, (Length(sName) - iAt))) to sTail
        Move (Length(sTail)) to iLast
        If (iLast = 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        For i from 1 to iLast
            If (Pos(Mid(sTail, 1, i), "0123456789") = 0) ;
                Function_Return False
        Loop
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    // The asAllNames element index whose name matches sNameLC case-insensitively, or -1.
    Function _StructIndexOf String[] ByRef asAllNames String sNameLC Returns Integer
        Integer i iLast
        Move (SizeOfArray(asAllNames) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Lowercase(asAllNames[i]) = sNameLC) ;
                Function_Return i
        Loop
        Function_Return -1
    End_Function

    /* Parse one projection function file (Win32API-NN.pkg) into aFns - APPENDED, so one array
       collects a whole clone. The generated shape, ported from the Python parser rule for rule:
       a head line 'External_Function <name> "<entry>" <dll> [;]' with NOTHING else on it, then
       body lines '<type> <name> [; // comment]' until 'Returns <type>' or a blank line. A
       declaration without a Returns is procedure-shaped and out of scope. When two files
       declare the same (dll,entry), the LAST parsed wins - dict semantics in the original. The
       last-wins is enforced at lookup (see _FindProjFn), not here. */
    Procedure ParseFunctionFile String[] ByRef asLines tW32ProjFn[] ByRef aFns
        tW32ProjFn Fn EmptyFn
        String[] asTok asBodyTok
        String sLine sBody sComment
        Integer i iLast iPos iTok
        Boolean bGotRet

        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        Move 0 to i
        While (i <= iLast)
            Send _Tokens asLines[i] (&asTok)
            Move (SizeOfArray(asTok)) to iTok
            If (iTok >= 4 and iTok <= 5 and Lowercase(asTok[0]) = "external_function" and ;
                _IsWordName(Self, asTok[1]) and ;
                Length(asTok[2]) >= 2 and Left(asTok[2], 1) = '"' and Right(asTok[2], 1) = '"' and ;
                (iTok = 4 or asTok[4] = ";")) Begin
                Move EmptyFn to Fn
                Move asTok[1] to Fn.sName
                Move (Mid(asTok[2], (Length(asTok[2]) - 2), 2)) to Fn.sEntry
                Move asTok[3] to Fn.sDll
                If (Right(Fn.sDll, 1) = ";") ;
                    Move (Left(Fn.sDll, (Length(Fn.sDll) - 1))) to Fn.sDll
                Move False to bGotRet
                Increment i
                While (i <= iLast)
                    Move asLines[i] to sLine
                    Increment i
                    If (Trim(sLine) = "") ;
                        Break
                    Move (Pos("//", sLine)) to iPos
                    Move "" to sComment
                    If (iPos > 0) Begin
                        Move (Trim(Mid(sLine, (Length(sLine)), (iPos + 2)))) to sComment
                        Move (Left(sLine, (iPos - 1))) to sBody
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Move sLine to sBody
                    End
                    Move (Replaces((Character(9)), sBody, " ")) to sBody
                    Move (Trim(sBody)) to sBody
                    While (Right(sBody, 1) = ";")
                        Move (Trim(Left(sBody, (Length(sBody) - 1)))) to sBody
                    Loop
                    If (sBody <> "") Begin
                        Send _Tokens sBody (&asBodyTok)
                        If (Lowercase(asBodyTok[0]) = "returns") Begin
                            If (SizeOfArray(asBodyTok) >= 2) Begin
                                Move asBodyTok[1] to Fn.sRet
                                Move sComment     to Fn.sRetComment
                                Move True to bGotRet
                            End
                            Break
                        End
                        Else Begin
                            Move asBodyTok[0] to Fn.asParamType[SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamType)]
                            If (SizeOfArray(asBodyTok) >= 2) Begin
                                Move (JoinTokensFrom(Self, &asBodyTok, 1)) to Fn.asParamName[SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamName)]
                            End
                            Else Begin
                                Move ("arg" + String(SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamName))) to Fn.asParamName[SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamName)]
                            End
                            Move sComment to Fn.asParamComment[SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamComment)]
                        End
                    End
                Loop
                If (bGotRet = True) ;
                    Move Fn to aFns[SizeOfArray(aFns)]
            End
            Else Begin
                Increment i
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* Parse one projection struct file (Win32Struct-NN.pkg): 'Struct <name>' ... 'End_Struct',
       comment-only lines dropped, each member line collapsed to '<type> <rest>  // <c-type>'
       with the SAME Pointer->Handle rule as parameters. FIRST declaration of a name wins -
       dict-with-guard semantics in the original. asNames/asBodies are appended in lockstep;
       bodies are the member lines joined with LF.

       Within this file only: walking every name so far is quadratic, and 15,206 structs make that a
       matter of minutes. Across files _KeepFirstStructs settles it once, after the last file. */
    Procedure ParseStructFile String[] ByRef asLines String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asBodies
        String[] asTok
        String sLine sName sBody sMember sComment
        Integer i iLast iPos j jLast iFirst
        Boolean bKnown

        Move (SizeOfArray(asNames)) to iFirst
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        Move "" to sName
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(Replaces((Character(9)), asLines[i], " "))) to sLine
            Send _Tokens sLine (&asTok)
            If (SizeOfArray(asTok) = 2 and Lowercase(asTok[0]) = "struct") Begin
                Move asTok[1] to sName
                Move "" to sBody
            End
            Else Begin
                If (Lowercase(sLine) = "end_struct") Begin
                    If (sName <> "") Begin
                        Move False to bKnown
                        Move (SizeOfArray(asNames) - 1) to jLast
                        For j from iFirst to jLast
                            If (Lowercase(asNames[j]) = Lowercase(sName)) ;
                                Move True to bKnown
                        Loop
                        If (bKnown = False) Begin
                            Move sName to asNames[SizeOfArray(asNames)]
                            Move sBody to asBodies[SizeOfArray(asBodies)]
                        End
                    End
                    Move "" to sName
                End
                Else Begin
                    If (sName <> "" and sLine <> "" and Left(sLine, 2) <> "//") Begin
                        Move (Pos("//", sLine)) to iPos
                        Move "" to sComment
                        Move sLine to sMember
                        If (iPos > 0) Begin
                            Move (Trim(Mid(sLine, (Length(sLine)), (iPos + 2)))) to sComment
                            Move (Left(sLine, (iPos - 1))) to sMember
                        End
                        Send _Tokens sMember (&asTok)
                        If (SizeOfArray(asTok) >= 2) Begin
                            Move (NormaliseType(Self, asTok[0], sComment)) to asTok[0]
                            Move (JoinTokensFrom(Self, &asTok, 0)) to sMember
                            If (sComment <> "") ;
                                Move (sMember + "  // " + sComment) to sMember
                        End
                        Else Begin
                            Move (Trim(sMember)) to sMember
                        End
                        If (sMember <> "") Begin
                            If (sBody = "") ;
                                Move sMember to sBody
                            Else ;
                                Move (sBody + (Character(10)) + sMember) to sBody
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // Identifier runs ([A-Za-z0-9_]+) in sText - the ref-token walk over C comments.
    Procedure _IdentTokens String sText String[] ByRef asToks
        String[] asNone
        String sCh sCur
        Integer i iLen iAsc

        Move asNone to asToks
        Move (Length(sText)) to iLen
        Move "" to sCur
        For i from 1 to iLen
            Move (Mid(sText, 1, i)) to sCh
            Move (Ascii(sCh)) to iAsc
            If ((iAsc >= 65 and iAsc <= 90) or (iAsc >= 97 and iAsc <= 122) or (iAsc >= 48 and iAsc <= 57) or sCh = "_") Begin
                Move (sCur + sCh) to sCur
            End
            Else Begin
                If (sCur <> "") ;
                    Move sCur to asToks[SizeOfArray(asToks)]
                Move "" to sCur
            End
        Loop
        If (sCur <> "") ;
            Move sCur to asToks[SizeOfArray(asToks)]
    End_Procedure

    // Lower-bound binary search over asSorted (lowercased entries, DFSTRICMP-sorted) for an
    // EXACT lowercase match. Returns True when present.
    Function _SortedContains String[] ByRef asSorted String sKey Returns Boolean
        String sMid
        Integer iLo iHi iMid

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sKey))) to sKey
        Move 0 to iLo
        Move (SizeOfArray(asSorted) - 1) to iHi
        While (iLo <= iHi)
            Move ((iLo + iHi) / 2) to iMid
            Move asSorted[iMid] to sMid
            If (sMid = sKey) ;
                Function_Return True
            If (sMid < sKey) ;
                Move (iMid + 1) to iLo
            Else ;
                Move (iMid - 1) to iHi
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    /* The struct a parameter's C comment says it POINTS AT, spelled as the comment spells it - "" when
       it says no such thing. One star only: "MENUITEMINFOA*" is what a caller hands a buffer to, while
       "ITEMIDLIST**" is a pointer to somebody else's pointer. asStructNamesLC as in FunctionRow. */
    Function _PointedAtStruct String sComment String[] ByRef asStructNamesLC Returns String
        String sName

        Move (Trim(sComment)) to sName
        If (Right(sName, 1) <> "*") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Left(sName, (Length(sName) - 1))) to sName
        If (Pos("*", sName) > 0 or Pos(" ", sName) > 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        If (_SortedContains(Self, &asStructNamesLC, sName)) ;
            Function_Return sName
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    /* One "dll|entry|DF|<declaration>" row. The declaration flattens to one line; the trailing
       "// refs: ..." names the structs its comments mention (WinAPIStructForApi's scan reads
       that tail; the emitters cut it). asStructNamesLC must be lowercased and sorted.

       "// args: 4=MENUITEMINFOA" follows it and says the same per PARAMETER, counted from 1. refs is
       about the whole function, so it cannot say which argument a struct belongs to: a thread-id buffer
       handed to CreateThread looked like a SECURITY_ATTRIBUTES, which is the FIRST parameter
       (2026-11-03). The converter reads this tail: _WinAPIArgStructOf.

       "// ptrs: 1=PSTR 2=UInteger*" comes FIRST, on an ...A or ...W row only, and keeps the C type of
       every parameter the declaration hands over as raw memory (a bare Pointer). It is what tells
       GetComputerNameA from GetComputerNameW: both declare "Pointer lpBuffer", so the DataFlex types
       agree, but one writes 8-bit text there and the other UTF-16. _AnsiWideRefusalReason compares
       the two rows' tails (2026-11-21). It goes before refs: all three readers stop at the next tail
       now, but the args reader once read to the end of the row, and an older build still does. */
    Function FunctionRow tW32ProjFn Fn String[] ByRef asStructNamesLC Returns String
        String[] asToks asRefs
        String sDecl sTok sArgs sPtrs sLast
        Integer i iLast j jLast k kLast
        Boolean bHave

        Move ('External_Function ' + Fn.sName + ' "' + Fn.sEntry + '" ' + Fn.sDll) to sDecl
        Move (SizeOfArray(Fn.asParamType) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (sDecl + " " + NormaliseType(Self, Fn.asParamType[i], Fn.asParamComment[i]) + " " + Fn.asParamName[i]) to sDecl
        Loop
        Move (sDecl + " Returns " + NormaliseReturn(Self, Fn.sRet, Fn.sRetComment)) to sDecl

        // ptrs: the C type behind each raw-memory parameter of an A/W entry. Case-sensitive on purpose:
        // the projection spells the suffix in capitals, and a lowercase "a" ends ordinary words.
        Move (Right(Fn.sEntry, 1)) to sLast
        If (sLast = "A" or sLast = "W") Begin
            Move "" to sPtrs
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (NormaliseType(Self, Fn.asParamType[i], Fn.asParamComment[i]) = "Pointer") Begin
                    Move (Trim(Replaces((Character(9)), Fn.asParamComment[i], " "))) to sTok
                    If (sTok <> "" and Pos(" ", sTok) = 0) ;
                        Move (sPtrs + " " + String(i + 1) + "=" + sTok) to sPtrs
                End
            Loop
            If (sPtrs <> "") ;
                Move (sDecl + " // ptrs:" + sPtrs) to sDecl
        End

        // refs: every identifier in the comments (params + return) naming a projection struct,
        // deduped in first-seen order, ORIGINAL casing kept.
        For i from 0 to (iLast + 1)
            If (i <= iLast) ;
                Send _IdentTokens Fn.asParamComment[i] (&asToks)
            Else ;
                Send _IdentTokens Fn.sRetComment (&asToks)
            Move (SizeOfArray(asToks) - 1) to jLast
            For j from 0 to jLast
                Move asToks[j] to sTok
                If (_SortedContains(Self, &asStructNamesLC, sTok)) Begin
                    Move False to bHave
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asRefs) - 1) to kLast
                    For k from 0 to kLast
                        If (asRefs[k] = sTok) ;
                            Move True to bHave
                    Loop
                    If (bHave = False) ;
                        Move sTok to asRefs[SizeOfArray(asRefs)]
                End
            Loop
        Loop
        Move (SizeOfArray(asRefs) - 1) to kLast
        If (kLast >= 0) Begin
            Move (sDecl + " // refs:") to sDecl
            For k from 0 to kLast
                Move (sDecl + " " + asRefs[k]) to sDecl
            Loop
            Move "" to sArgs
            For i from 0 to iLast
                Get _PointedAtStruct Fn.asParamComment[i] (&asStructNamesLC) to sTok
                If (sTok <> "") ;
                    Move (sArgs + " " + String(i + 1) + "=" + sTok) to sArgs
            Loop
            If (sArgs <> "") ;
                Move (sDecl + " // args:" + sArgs) to sDecl
        End
        Function_Return (Lowercase(Fn.sDll) + "|" + Lowercase(Fn.sEntry) + "|DF|" + sDecl)
    End_Function

    // One "NAME|DF|Struct ...\n...\nEnd_Struct" row; the NAME key uppercased, the body verbatim.
    Function StructRow String sName String sBody Returns String
        Function_Return (Uppercase(sName) + "|DF|" + "Struct " + sName + (Character(10)) + sBody + (Character(10)) + "End_Struct")
    End_Function

    /* The first declaration of each struct name across all files, the others dropped, the order kept.
       Sorted on "<lowercase name> <index>" with the index zero-padded so equal names sort by it; a space
       because DataFlex compares through its collation table, where a control character would not order
       below a digit (Hrv_IndexFindsPrefixFamilyBase). */
    Procedure _KeepFirstStructs String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asBodies
        String[] asPack asOutNames asOutBodies
        Boolean[] abDrop
        String sThis sPrev sIdx
        Integer i iLast iPos

        Move (SizeOfArray(asNames) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(asNames[i]) + " " + Right("0000000" + String(i), 7)) to asPack[i]
            Move False to abDrop[i]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asPack, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asPack
        Move "" to sPrev
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Pos(" ", asPack[i])) to iPos
            Move (Left(asPack[i], (iPos - 1))) to sThis
            If (sThis = sPrev) Begin
                Move (Right(asPack[i], 7)) to sIdx
                Move True to abDrop[Integer(sIdx)]
            End
            Move sThis to sPrev
        Loop
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (abDrop[i] = False) Begin
                Move asNames[i]  to asOutNames[SizeOfArray(asOutNames)]
                Move asBodies[i] to asOutBodies[SizeOfArray(asOutBodies)]
            End
        Loop
        Move asOutNames  to asNames
        Move asOutBodies to asBodies
    End_Procedure

    // The rows of asNew whose identity asExisting does not hold yet, for a merge that may only add.
    Procedure _RowsNotCarried String[] ByRef asExisting String[] ByRef asNew Integer iKeyFields String[] ByRef asOut
        String[] asKeys asNone
        Integer i iLast

        Move asNone to asOut
        Move (SizeOfArray(asExisting) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (WinApiRowKey(asExisting[i], iKeyFields)) to asKeys[i]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asKeys, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asKeys
        Move (SizeOfArray(asNew) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (_SortedContains(Self, &asKeys, WinApiRowKey(asNew[i], iKeyFields)) = False) ;
                Move asNew[i] to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* Merge: harvested identity replaces, everything else stays, output KEY-sorted. The sort
       packs key + CS_S + index so that a key which is a PREFIX of another still sorts
       before it (a full-row compare would put "getdc|..." AFTER "getdcex|..." because '|'
       outranks 'e' - the Python tool sorted by key alone, and the file should diff clean). */
    Procedure MergeRows String[] ByRef asExisting String[] ByRef asNew Integer iKeyFields String[] ByRef asOut Integer ByRef iKept
        String[] asNewKeys asAll asPack asNone
        String sKey
        Integer i iLast iPos

        Move asNone to asOut
        Move 0 to iKept
        Move (SizeOfArray(asNew) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (WinApiRowKey(asNew[i], iKeyFields)) to asNewKeys[SizeOfArray(asNewKeys)]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asNewKeys, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asNewKeys

        Move (SizeOfArray(asExisting) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (WinApiRowKey(asExisting[i], iKeyFields)) to sKey
            If (_SortedContains(Self, &asNewKeys, sKey) = False) Begin
                Move asExisting[i] to asAll[SizeOfArray(asAll)]
                Increment iKept
            End
        Loop
        Move (SizeOfArray(asNew) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move asNew[i] to asAll[SizeOfArray(asAll)]
        Loop

        Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (WinApiRowKey(asAll[i], iKeyFields) + (CS_S) + String(i)) to asPack[SizeOfArray(asPack)]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asPack, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asPack
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move asPack[i] to sKey
            Move (RightPos((CS_S), sKey)) to iPos
            Move (Right(sKey, (Length(sKey) - iPos))) to sKey
            Move asAll[Integer(sKey)] to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* The projection lookup index: "dll|entry" + Chr(1) + element-index, sorted. Duplicate
       (dll,entry) pairs are legal in the clone (one API in two topic folders); the ORIGINAL
       tool's dict made the LAST parsed win, so _FindProjFn walks equal keys and answers the
       highest index. */
    Procedure BuildFnIndex tW32ProjFn[] ByRef aFns String[] ByRef asIdx
        String[] asNone
        Integer i iLast

        Move asNone to asIdx
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFns) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(aFns[i].sDll) + "|" + Lowercase(aFns[i].sEntry) + (CS_S) + String(i)) to asIdx[SizeOfArray(asIdx)]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asIdx, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asIdx
    End_Procedure

    // The aFns element index for "dll|entry" (lowercased), or -1. Last-parsed wins (see above).
    Function _FindProjFn String[] ByRef asIdx String sKey Returns Integer
        String sMid sPre
        Integer iLo iHi iMid iBest iPos iLen

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sKey)) + (CS_S)) to sPre
        Move (Length(sPre)) to iLen
        Move 0 to iLo
        Move (SizeOfArray(asIdx) - 1) to iHi
        // lower-bound on the prefix...
        While (iLo < iHi)
            Move ((iLo + iHi) / 2) to iMid
            Move (Lowercase(Left(asIdx[iMid], iLen))) to sMid
            If (sMid < sPre) ;
                Move (iMid + 1) to iLo
            Else ;
                Move iMid to iHi
        Loop
        Move -1 to iBest
        // ...then walk the equal-key run, keeping the HIGHEST element index (last-parsed wins).
        While (iLo <= (SizeOfArray(asIdx) - 1))
            Move asIdx[iLo] to sMid
            If (Lowercase(Left(sMid, iLen)) <> sPre) ;
                Break
            Move (RightPos((CS_S), sMid)) to iPos
            Move (Right(sMid, (Length(sMid) - iPos))) to sMid
            If (Integer(sMid) > iBest) ;
                Move (Integer(sMid)) to iBest
            Increment iLo
        Loop
        Function_Return iBest
    End_Function

    /* The corpus intersection: for each entry point the workspace scan found
       (AppSrc\WindowsAPI.json "functions"), try the name itself, then name+w, then name+a -
       EVERY candidate the projection covers is taken (that is how both ShellExecuteW and
       ShellExecuteA arrive from one corpus name), each (dll,entry) at most once. Returns False
       with sErr set when the corpus file cannot be read. */
    Function CorpusSelect String sCorpusJson tW32ProjFn[] ByRef aFns String[] ByRef asIdx tW32ProjFn[] ByRef aChosen String ByRef sErr Returns Boolean
        Handle hoJson hoFuncs hoOne
        String[] asChosenKeys
        String sName sDll sCand sKey
        UChar[] ucData
        Integer i iMax iCh c iHit
        Boolean bOK

        Move "" to sErr
        Get vFilePathExists sCorpusJson to bOK
        If (bOK = False) Begin
            Move ("Corpus file not found: " + sCorpusJson) to sErr
            Function_Return False
        End
        Get rfOpenInput sCorpusJson to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) Begin
            Move ("Corpus file could not be opened: " + sCorpusJson) to sErr
            Function_Return False
        End
        Read_Block channel iCh ucData -1
        Move (rfStripUtf8Bom(ucData)) to ucData
        Send rfCloseInput iCh
        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
        Set pbRequireAllMembers of hoJson to False
        Get ParseUtf8 of hoJson ucData to bOK
        If (bOK = False) Begin
            Send Destroy of hoJson
            Move ("Corpus file did not parse as JSON: " + sCorpusJson) to sErr
            Function_Return False
        End
        Get MemberEnh of hoJson "functions" to hoFuncs
        If (hoFuncs = 0) Begin
            Send Destroy of hoJson
            Move ("Corpus file has no 'functions' member: " + sCorpusJson) to sErr
            Function_Return False
        End
        Set pbRequireAllMembers of hoFuncs to False
        Get MemberCount of hoFuncs to iMax
        Decrement iMax
        For i from 0 to iMax
            Get MemberNameByIndex of hoFuncs i to sName
            Get MemberEnh of hoFuncs sName to hoOne
            Move "" to sDll
            If (hoOne <> 0) Begin
                Set pbRequireAllMembers of hoOne to False
                Get MemberValueEnh of hoOne "dll" to sDll
                Send Destroy of hoOne
            End
            If (Trim(sDll) <> "") Begin
                Move (Lowercase(Trim(sDll))) to sDll
                If (not(sDll contains ".")) ;
                    Move (sDll + ".dll") to sDll
                For c from 0 to 2
                    Move (Lowercase(Trim(sName))) to sCand
                    If (c = 1) ;
                        Move (sCand + "w") to sCand
                    If (c = 2) ;
                        Move (sCand + "a") to sCand
                    Move (sDll + "|" + sCand) to sKey
                    Get _FindProjFn (&asIdx) sKey to iHit
                    If (iHit >= 0) Begin
                        If (_PlainContains(Self, &asChosenKeys, sKey) = False) Begin
                            Move sKey to asChosenKeys[SizeOfArray(asChosenKeys)]
                            Move aFns[iHit] to aChosen[SizeOfArray(aChosen)]
                        End
                    End
                Loop
            End
        Loop
        Send Destroy of hoFuncs
        Send Destroy of hoJson
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    /* The struct closure: every struct a chosen function's comments name, then every struct
       type among THOSE structs' members, to a fixed point. asNamesLC is the sorted lowercase
       name index over ALL projection structs; asNeededLC comes back lowercase. */
    Procedure StructClosure tW32ProjFn[] ByRef aChosen String[] ByRef asNamesLC String[] ByRef asAllNames String[] ByRef asAllBodies String[] ByRef asNeededLC
        String[] asToks asBodyLines asNone
        String sTok sT0
        Integer i iLast j jLast k kLast n nLast iGrow iPos

        Move asNone to asNeededLC
        Move (SizeOfArray(aChosen) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (SizeOfArray(aChosen[i].asParamComment) - 1) to jLast
            For j from 0 to (jLast + 1)
                If (j <= jLast) ;
                    Send _IdentTokens aChosen[i].asParamComment[j] (&asToks)
                Else ;
                    Send _IdentTokens aChosen[i].sRetComment (&asToks)
                Move (SizeOfArray(asToks) - 1) to kLast
                For k from 0 to kLast
                    Move (Lowercase(asToks[k])) to sTok
                    If (_SortedContains(Self, &asNamesLC, sTok)) Begin
                        If (_PlainContains(Self, &asNeededLC, sTok) = False) ;
                            Move sTok to asNeededLC[SizeOfArray(asNeededLC)]
                    End
                Loop
            Loop
        Loop
        // frontier expansion: member TYPES that are themselves projection structs
        Move 1 to iGrow
        While (iGrow > 0)
            Move 0 to iGrow
            Move (SizeOfArray(asNeededLC) - 1) to iLast
            For i from 0 to iLast
                Move (_StructIndexOf(Self, &asAllNames, asNeededLC[i])) to j
                If (j >= 0) Begin
                    Move (StrSplitToArray(asAllBodies[j], (Character(10)))) to asBodyLines
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asBodyLines) - 1) to nLast
                    For n from 0 to nLast
                        Send _Tokens asBodyLines[n] (&asToks)
                        If (SizeOfArray(asToks) >= 1) Begin
                            Move (Lowercase(asToks[0])) to sT0
                            Move (Pos("[", sT0)) to iPos
                            If (iPos > 0) ;
                                Move (Left(sT0, (iPos - 1))) to sT0
                            If (_SortedContains(Self, &asNamesLC, sT0)) Begin
                                If (_PlainContains(Self, &asNeededLC, sT0) = False) Begin
                                    Move sT0 to asNeededLC[SizeOfArray(asNeededLC)]
                                    Increment iGrow
                                End
                            End
                        End
                    Loop
                End
            Loop
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // The clone's short commit sha + today's date, via .git plumbing (no git.exe needed):
    // HEAD holds "ref: <path>" -> that file's first line is the sha; a detached HEAD holds it
    // directly. "" when the clone has no readable .git.
    Function GitStamp String sCloneRoot Returns String
        String[] asLines
        String sHead sSha sToday
        DateTime dtNow
        Date dNow

        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(vFolderFormat(sCloneRoot) + ".git\HEAD")) to asLines
        If (SizeOfArray(asLines) = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(asLines[0])) to sHead
        If (Lowercase(Left(sHead, 4)) = "ref:") Begin
            Move (Trim(Mid(sHead, (Length(sHead)), 5))) to sHead
            Move (Replaces("/", sHead, "\")) to sHead
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(vFolderFormat(sCloneRoot) + ".git\" + sHead)) to asLines
            If (SizeOfArray(asLines) = 0) ;
                Function_Return ""
            Move (Trim(asLines[0])) to sHead
        End
        Move (Left(sHead, 7)) to sSha
        Move (CurrentDateTime()) to dtNow
        Move dtNow to dNow
        Move (String(DateGetYear(dNow)) + "-" + Right("0" + String(DateGetMonth(dNow)), 2) + "-" + Right("0" + String(DateGetDay(dNow)), 2)) to sToday
        Function_Return (sSha + " " + sToday)
    End_Function

    /* Write one catalogue JSON: {iVersion, asRows, _meta_harvest{source, sourceCommit,
       harvested, kept}} - the same shape and key names the Python tool wrote, so nothing
       reading the file can tell the tools apart. Attribution is a condition of taking the
       data. Returns False when the file cannot be written. */
    Function WriteCatalogWithMeta String sPath String[] ByRef asRows Integer iHarvested Integer iKept String sSourceCommit Returns Boolean
        Handle hoDoc hoMeta
        UChar[] ucJson
        Integer iCh
        tWinAPICatalogFile TheFile

        Move CI_WinAPICatalogVersion to TheFile.iVersion
        Move asRows to TheFile.asRows
        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoDoc
        Send DataTypeToJson of hoDoc TheFile
        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoMeta
        Send InitializeJsonType of hoMeta jsonTypeObject
        Send SetMemberValue of hoMeta "source" jsonTypeString "Win32_DataFlex_Projection (Frank Cheng, MIT) - generated from Microsoft win32metadata"
        Send SetMemberValue of hoMeta "sourceCommit" jsonTypeString sSourceCommit
        Send SetMemberValue of hoMeta "harvested" jsonTypeInteger iHarvested
        Send SetMemberValue of hoMeta "kept" jsonTypeInteger iKept
        Send SetMember of hoDoc "_meta_harvest" hoMeta
        Set peWhiteSpace of hoDoc to jpWhitespace_Pretty
        Get StringifyUtf8 of hoDoc to ucJson
        Send Destroy of hoDoc
        Get rfOpenOutput sPath to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        Write channel iCh ucJson
        Send rfCloseOutput iCh
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    /* THE WHOLE HARVEST, paths explicit. Reads the clone (Win32API-*.pkg / Win32Struct-*.pkg,
       recursively), selects (corpus intersection, or everything when pbHarvestAll), closes over
       the structs (pbHarvestAll: takes them all), merges into the two catalogue files, and reports. Returns False with the
       report carrying the reason when nothing could be done; True with the counts otherwise. */
    Function HarvestClone String sCloneRoot String sCorpusJson String sFnJson String sStructJson String ByRef sReport Returns Boolean
        tW32ProjFn[] aFns aChosen
        tRFSearchResult[] aFiles
        String[] asLines asIdx asStNames asStBodies asStNamesLC asNeededLC asFnRows asStRows asExisting asMerged
        String[] asAliasRows asStAdded
        String sErr sStamp sCRLF sAliasNote
        Handle hoStore
        Integer i iLast iKept1 iKept2 iIdx iKeptA iGenerated
        Boolean bOK bAll

        Move (Character(13) + Character(10)) to sCRLF
        Move "" to sReport
        Get pbHarvestAll to bAll
        If (rfDirectoryExists(sCloneRoot) = False) Begin
            Move ("Clone folder not found: " + sCloneRoot) to sReport
            Function_Return False
        End

        // parse the clone
        Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sCloneRoot) + "Win32API-*.pkg"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFiles
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFiles) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(aFiles[i].sFilename)) to asLines
            Send ParseFunctionFile (&asLines) (&aFns)
        Loop
        Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sCloneRoot) + "Win32Struct-*.pkg"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFiles
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFiles) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(aFiles[i].sFilename)) to asLines
            Send ParseStructFile (&asLines) (&asStNames) (&asStBodies)
        Loop
        Send _KeepFirstStructs (&asStNames) (&asStBodies)
        If (SizeOfArray(aFns) = 0) Begin
            Move ("No Win32API-*.pkg declarations found under: " + sCloneRoot) to sReport
            Function_Return False
        End
        Move ("projection: " + String(SizeOfArray(aFns)) + " functions, " + String(SizeOfArray(asStNames)) + " structs") to sReport

        // sorted lowercase struct-name index
        Move (SizeOfArray(asStNames) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(asStNames[i])) to asStNamesLC[SizeOfArray(asStNamesLC)]
        Loop
        Move (SortArray(asStNamesLC, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to asStNamesLC

        // selection
        Send BuildFnIndex (&aFns) (&asIdx)
        If (bAll = True) Begin
            Move aFns to aChosen
        End
        Else Begin
            Get CorpusSelect sCorpusJson (&aFns) (&asIdx) (&aChosen) (&sErr) to bOK
            If (bOK = False) Begin
                Move (sReport + sCRLF + sErr) to sReport
                Function_Return False
            End
        End
        Move (sReport + sCRLF + "chosen: " + String(SizeOfArray(aChosen)) + " function(s)") to sReport

        // struct closure + rows
        Move (SizeOfArray(aChosen) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (FunctionRow(Self, aChosen[i], &asStNamesLC)) to asFnRows[SizeOfArray(asFnRows)]
        Loop
        Move 0 to iGenerated
        If (bAll = True) Begin
            Move (SizeOfArray(asStNames) - 1) to iLast
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (_IsGeneratedStructName(Self, asStNames[i])) ;
                    Increment iGenerated
                Else ;
                    Move (StructRow(Self, asStNames[i], asStBodies[i])) to asStRows[SizeOfArray(asStRows)]
            Loop
            Move (sReport + sCRLF + "all structs: " + String(SizeOfArray(asStRows)) + " named, " + String(iGenerated) + " generated left out") to sReport
        End
        Else Begin
            Send StructClosure (&aChosen) (&asStNamesLC) (&asStNames) (&asStBodies) (&asNeededLC)
            Move (sReport + sCRLF + "struct closure: " + String(SizeOfArray(asNeededLC)) + " struct(s)") to sReport
            Move (SizeOfArray(asNeededLC) - 1) to iLast
            For i from 0 to iLast
                Move (_StructIndexOf(Self, &asStNames, asNeededLC[i])) to iIdx
                If (iIdx >= 0) Begin
                    If (_IsGeneratedStructName(Self, asStNames[iIdx]) = False) ;
                        Move (StructRow(Self, asStNames[iIdx], asStBodies[iIdx])) to asStRows[SizeOfArray(asStRows)]
                End
            Loop
        End

        // merge + write, with provenance
        Get GitStamp sCloneRoot to sStamp
        Get Create (RefClass(cWinAPICatalogStore)) to hoStore
        Get LoadCatalog of hoStore sFnJson to asExisting
        Send MergeRows (&asExisting) (&asFnRows) 2 (&asMerged) (&iKept1)
        /* THE BARE ALIASES RIDE WITH THE HARVEST (2026-09-12) - measured on the MERGED set, so a
           bare row the projection carries is seen and left alone, and merged by the same rule, so a
           re-run finds its own rows and adds nothing. See BareAliasRows. */
        Get BareAliasRows (&asMerged) (&sAliasNote) to asAliasRows
        If (SizeOfArray(asAliasRows) > 0) Begin
            Move asMerged to asExisting
            Send MergeRows (&asExisting) (&asAliasRows) 2 (&asMerged) (&iKeptA)
        End
        Get WriteCatalogWithMeta sFnJson (&asMerged) (SizeOfArray(asFnRows)) iKept1 sStamp to bOK
        If (bOK = False) Begin
            Send Destroy of hoStore
            Move (sReport + sCRLF + "COULD NOT WRITE: " + sFnJson) to sReport
            Function_Return False
        End
        Move (sReport + sCRLF + "functions: " + String(SizeOfArray(asFnRows)) + " harvested + " + String(iKept1) + " kept -> " + sFnJson) to sReport
        Move (sReport + sCRLF + sAliasNote) to sReport
        Get LoadCatalog of hoStore sStructJson to asExisting
        Send _RowsNotCarried (&asExisting) (&asStRows) 1 (&asStAdded)
        Send MergeRows (&asExisting) (&asStAdded) 1 (&asMerged) (&iKept2)
        Get WriteCatalogWithMeta sStructJson (&asMerged) (SizeOfArray(asStAdded)) iKept2 sStamp to bOK
        Send Destroy of hoStore
        If (bOK = False) Begin
            Move (sReport + sCRLF + "COULD NOT WRITE: " + sStructJson) to sReport
            Function_Return False
        End
        Move (sReport + sCRLF + "structs  : " + String(SizeOfArray(asStAdded)) + " added + " + String(iKept2) + " kept as they were -> " + sStructJson) to sReport
        Move (sReport + sCRLF + "source commit: " + sStamp) to sReport
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    // The module handle for one dll, loaded once per run. asDll / ahMod are the caller's cache and
    // move in lockstep; a dll that will not load is remembered as 0, so it is not retried per row.
    Function _AliasModule String sDll String[] ByRef asDll Handle[] ByRef ahMod Returns Handle
        String sLow
        Handle hMod
        Integer iAt

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sDll))) to sLow
        Move (SearchArray(sLow, asDll)) to iAt
        If (iAt <> -1) ;
            Function_Return ahMod[iAt]
        Move (LoadLibrary(sLow)) to hMod
        Move sLow to asDll[SizeOfArray(asDll)]
        Move hMod to ahMod[SizeOfArray(ahMod)]
        Function_Return hMod
    End_Function

    /* WHICH TWIN A BARE EXPORT IS - "a", "w", or "" for neither. Windows answers it itself: the bare
       name and a twin resolve to the SAME ADDRESS when the bare name is an alias of that twin, and
       to different ones when the bare export is a function in its own right (PlaySound, the tapi32
       family). "" also covers a bare name the dll does not export at all - a declaration naming one
       cannot bind, and DataFlex raises Error 4355 on the first call.

       THE NAME MUST CARRY ITS REAL CASE: GetProcAddress matches export names byte for byte, and the
       catalogue's key field is lowercased - so the caller passes the spelling from the declaration.

       AND IT MUST BE THE LOADER'S ANSWER, not the export table's. A cross-check that read the export
       RVAs directly disagreed on one name: sfc.dll forwards SRSetRestorePoint and SRSetRestorePointA
       both to sfc_os.SRSetRestorePointA, so their forwarder STRINGS differ while the function does
       not. GetProcAddress resolves the forwarder, which is exactly what binding a declaration does. */
    Function _BareExportTwin Handle hMod String sBareCased Returns String
        LongPtr lpBare lpTwin

        If (hMod = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        If (Trim(sBareCased) = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (HarvGetProcAddress(hMod, sBareCased)) to lpBare
        If (lpBare = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (HarvGetProcAddress(hMod, (sBareCased + "A"))) to lpTwin
        If (lpBare = lpTwin) ;
            Function_Return "a"
        Move (HarvGetProcAddress(hMod, (sBareCased + "W"))) to lpTwin
        If (lpBare = lpTwin) ;
            Function_Return "w"
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    // The entry point as the row SPELLS it - the text between the row's first pair of quotes, which
    // is the declaration's own entry. "" when the row carries no quoted entry.
    Function _RowEntryCased String sRow Returns String
        Integer iOpen iClose

        Move (Pos('"', sRow)) to iOpen
        If (iOpen = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Pos('"', sRow, (iOpen + 1))) to iClose
        If (iClose <= iOpen) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Mid(sRow, (iClose - iOpen - 1), (iOpen + 1)))
    End_Function

    // The same row under the BARE key: the flavour and the declaration ride along verbatim, so the
    // body still names the function that is really bound. The retyper reads only types from it, and
    // keeps the local declaration's own name and entry (_ApiDeclWithSdkTypes: "positions 0-3 are
    // the head, verbatim"), so nothing rewrites the caller's spelling.
    Function _AliasRowOf String sRow String sBareLower Returns String
        Integer i1 i2

        Move (Pos("|", sRow)) to i1
        If (i1 = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Pos("|", sRow, (i1 + 1))) to i2
        If (i2 <= i1) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Left(sRow, i1) + sBareLower + Right(sRow, (Length(sRow) - i2 + 1)))
    End_Function

    /* THE BARE ALIAS ROWS, MEASURED (Nils 2026-09-12, asking why a bare External_Function was
       offered no fix).

       Windows exports a text API as ...A and ...W; the bare name is a C macro, not an export - except
       where a dll keeps a bare ALIAS for compatibility, and that is exactly what legacy DataFlex code
       declares (Shell_NotifyIcon, ShellExecuteEx, lstrcpy). The catalogue is harvested under the SDK
       spellings, so the lookup answered a bare name by APPENDING "a", then "w": a spelling rule, not
       a fact. Measured against the dlls, that rule is wrong for real exports - kernel32's bare
       ReplaceFile IS ReplaceFileW, shell32's ILCreateFromPath and IsLFNDrive are W as well, and
       PlaySound and the tapi32 family are functions of their own. Every such declaration was being
       judged against the A prototype, silently.

       So the catalogue carries the answer instead: a row under the bare key when - and only when -
       the bare export resolves to the SAME ADDRESS as the ...A entry. The body is the A row verbatim,
       because that IS the function being bound. A bare export that turns out to be the W twin gets NO
       row: a declaration of it then finds nothing and is left alone, which is right, because moving a
       call to wide marshalling is a separate decision and not the retyper's. Nor does one the dll
       does not export at all - that declaration cannot bind in the first place.

       ONLY WHERE THE CATALOGUE IS SILENT. A bare row the projection already carries is left exactly
       as it is: 157 of those exist and 27 carry types matching NEITHER twin, so copying a twin over
       them would destroy harvested data. Re-running adds nothing - the second run finds its own rows.

       THE ADDRESSES ARE THIS MACHINE'S. Only equality is stored, never an address, and these aliases
       are decades-old compatibility exports - but re-measuring means running a harvest on the other
       Windows build, not editing a row by hand. */
    Function BareAliasRows String[] ByRef asExisting String ByRef sReport Returns String[]
        String[] asOut asKeys asDll asWide
        Handle[] ahMod
        String sRow sDll sEntry sBareLow sBareCased sTwin
        Integer i iLast i1 i2 iHave iNone
        Handle hMod

        Move "" to sReport
        Move (SizeOfArray(asExisting) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (WinApiRowKey(asExisting[i], 2)) to asKeys[i]
        Loop
        // Plain sort, plain compare: the keys are lowercase by construction, which is the one
        // ordering _SortedContains reads them with.
        Move (SortArray(asKeys)) to asKeys
        Move 0 to iHave
        Move 0 to iNone
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move asExisting[i] to sRow
            Move (Pos("|", sRow)) to i1
            Move (Pos("|", sRow, (i1 + 1))) to i2
            If (i1 > 1) Begin
                If (i2 > (i1 + 1)) Begin
                    Move (Left(sRow, (i1 - 1))) to sDll
                    Move (Lowercase(Mid(sRow, (i2 - i1 - 1), (i1 + 1)))) to sEntry
                    Move "" to sBareLow
                    If (Right(sEntry, 1) = "a") ;
                        Move (Left(sEntry, (Length(sEntry) - 1))) to sBareLow
                    If (sBareLow <> "") Begin
                        If (_SortedContains(Self, &asKeys, (sDll + "|" + sBareLow + "|")) = True) ;
                            Increment iHave
                        Else If (_SortedContains(Self, &asKeys, (sDll + "|" + sBareLow + "w|")) = True) Begin
                            Move (_RowEntryCased(Self, sRow)) to sBareCased
                            If (sBareCased <> "") ;
                                Move (Left(sBareCased, (Length(sBareCased) - 1))) to sBareCased
                            Move (_AliasModule(Self, sDll, &asDll, &ahMod)) to hMod
                            Move (_BareExportTwin(Self, hMod, sBareCased)) to sTwin
                            If (sTwin = "a") ;
                                Move (_AliasRowOf(Self, sRow, sBareLow)) to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
                            Else If (sTwin = "w") ;
                                Move (sDll + "|" + sBareLow) to asWide[SizeOfArray(asWide)]
                            Else ;
                                Increment iNone
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
        Move ("bare aliases: " + String(SizeOfArray(asOut)) + " measured and added; " ;
            + String(SizeOfArray(asWide)) + " bare exports are the WIDE twin (left out on purpose); " ;
            + String(iNone) + " not exported bare, or their own code; " ;
            + String(iHave) + " already carried a row of their own") to sReport
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

End_Class
